---
import Placeholder from './Placeholder.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const privacyHref = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}${site.privacyUrl}`;
---
<section class="section faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="section-rule"></div>
    <h2 id="faq-title" class="display h2 c-text">Questions</h2>
    <dl class="faq-list c-text">
      <div>
        <dt>What is Anybody Is Genius?</dt>
        <dd>
          An AI teacher for adults. You choose what you want to understand. It checks what you
          already know, teaches one step past it, asks you to do the thinking, and brings ideas
          back over time. It isn’t a course library, and it isn’t a chatbot that just hands you
          answers.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Who is it for?</dt>
        <dd>
          Adults who want to understand things properly, whether they’re starting from nothing
          or already know a field well. It starts wherever you are.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Is the demo above the real app?</dt>
        <dd>
          No. It’s a fixed example, written and fact-checked by hand, to show the idea: one
          question taught at five depths. The app finds your level and adjusts as you go, rather
          than picking from five set answers.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>When does it launch?</dt>
        <dd>
          Early access opens {site.launchDate ?? <Placeholder label="launch date" />}. People on
          the list get the first invitations.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>What happens to my email?</dt>
        <dd>
          We use it for one thing: early access. You’ll get one email when your invitation is
          ready, and at most one short note a month before then. We don’t sell it or share it
          with advertisers. Every email has an unsubscribe link, and the
          <a href={privacyHref}>privacy policy</a> has the details.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq-list { margin-top: calc(var(--u) * 5); max-width: 33em; }
  .faq-list > div { padding-block: calc(var(--u) * 3); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .faq-list > div:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  dt { font-family: var(--f-display); font-size: var(--s-24); line-height: calc(var(--u) * 4); }
  dd { margin-top: calc(var(--u) * 1); text-wrap: pretty; }
</style>
